---
title: "decryptSealedBid (LegionSealedBidAuctionSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_key: caller decrypts a sealed bid
    q_check_key --> q_check_position: privateKey has been published
    q_check_key --> q_revert_no_key: private key not yet released
    q_check_position --> q_decrypt: investor has encrypted bid data
    q_check_position --> q_revert_no_bid: no bid to decrypt
    q_decrypt --> q_verify: decryptedAmount = ECIES.decrypt(privateKey, encryptedAmountOut, salt)
    q_verify --> [*]: return decryptedAmount
    q_revert_no_key --> [*]: revert PrivateKeyNotPublished
    q_revert_no_bid --> [*]: revert NoBidData

    note right of q_decrypt
        INV-001: Decryption is a public view function (anyone can verify bids)
        INV-002: salt must equal investor address for valid decryption
        INV-003: Decrypted amount represents investor's desired token allocation
    end note
